0-approve}. NOTE: If `amount` is the maximum `uint256`, the allowance is not updated on `transferFrom`. This is semantically equivalent to an infinite approval. Requirements: - `spender` cannot be the zero address."},"asset()":{"details":"See {IERC4626-asset}. "},"balance()":{"details":"Retrieve the amount of assets in the strategy pool."},"balanceOf(address)":{"details":"See {IERC20-balanceOf}."},"convertToAssets(uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC4626-convertToAssets}. "},"convertToShares(uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC4626-convertToShares}. "},"currentManagementFee()":{"details":"Retrieve the current total amount of management fee share tokens, including those that are yet to be minted."},"decimals()":{"details":"Decimals are read from the underlying asset in the constructor and cached. If this fails (e.g., the asset has not been created yet), the cached value is set to a default obtained by `super.decimals()` (which depends on inheritance but is most likely 18). Override this function in order to set a guaranteed hardcoded value. See {IERC20Metadata-decimals}."},"decreaseAllowance(address,uint256)":{"details":"Atomically decreases the allowance granted to `spender` by the caller. This is an alternative to {approve} that can be used as a mitigation for problems described in {IERC20-approve}. Emits an {Approval} event indicating the updated allowance. Requirements: - `spender` cannot be the zero address. - `spender` must have allowance for the caller of at least `subtractedValue`."},"deleverageWithdraw(uint8,address,uint256,bytes,uint256,uint256,address,address)":{"details":"When there is insufficient idle funds in the strategy pool, users can opt to withdraw funds and reduce leverage in a specific lending protocol.","params":{"_assets":"The original amount of assets that could be redeemed.","_flashloanSelector":"The selection of the flash loan protocol.","_owner":"The owner of the redeemed share tokens.","_protocolId":"The index number of the lending protocol.","_receiver":"The address of the recipient for the redeemed assets.","_swapData":"The calldata for the 1inch exchange operation.","_swapGetMin":"The minimum amount of token to be obtained during the 1inch exchange operation.","_token":"The type of token to be redeemed."},"returns":{"shares":"The amount of share tokens obtained."}},"deposit(uint256,address)":{"details":"The deposit method of ERC4626, with the parameter being the amount of assets.","params":{"_assets":"The amount of stETH being deposited.","_receiver":"The recipient of the share tokens."},"returns":{"shares":"The amount of share tokens obtained."}},"getDeleverageWithdrawAmount(uint256,bool,uint8)":{"details":"Retrieve the amount of stETH required for performing a swap during the withdrawal for reducing leverage.","params":{"_isETH":"\"True\" indicates that ETH is being withdrawn, otherwise it is stETH.","_stETHAmount":"The amount of stETH to be withdrawn if leverage is not being reduced."},"returns":{"amount":"The amount of stETH required for the swap."}},"getDeleverageWithdrawFee(uint256)":{"details":"Retrieve the amount of the exit fee for reducing leverage.","params":{"_stETHAmount":"The amount of stETH to be withdrawn."},"returns":{"_0":"The exit fee to be deducted."}},"getVersion()":{"details":"Retrieve the version number of the vault contract."},"getWithdrawFee(uint256)":{"details":"Retrieve the amount of the exit fee.","params":{"_stETHAmount":"The amount of stETH to be withdrawn."},"returns":{"_0":"The exit fee to be deducted."}},"increaseAllowance(address,uint256)":{"details":"Atomically increases the allowance granted to `spender` by the caller. This is an alternative to {approve} that can be used as a mitigation for problems described in {IERC20-approve}. Emits an {Approval} event indicating the updated allowance. Requirements: - `spender` cannot be the zero address."},"initialize(address,address,uint256,uint256,uint256,uint256)":{"details":"Initialize various parameters of the Vault contract.","params":{"_deleverageExitFeeRate":"The percentage of exit fee for reducing leverage.","_exitFeeRate":"The percentage of exit fee.","_feeReceiver":"The address of the recipient for management fees.","_managementFeePercentage":"The annualized management fee rate.","_marketCapacity":"The maximum investment capacity.","_strategy":"The contract address of the strategy pool, which manages all the assets."}},"managementFeeClaim()":{"details":"Redeem the corresponding assets using the management fee share tokens."},"managementFeeSettle()":{"details":"Mint management fee share tokens."},"maxDeposit(address)":{"details":"See {IERC4626-maxDeposit}. "},"maxMint(address)":{"details":"See {IERC4626-maxMint}. "},"maxRedeem(address)":{"details":"See {IERC4626-maxRedeem}. "},"maxWithdraw(address)":{"details":"See {IERC4626-maxWithdraw}. "},"mint(uint256,address)":{"details":"The deposit method of ERC4626, with the parameter being the amount of share tokens.","params":{"_receiver":"The recipient of the share tokens.","_shares":"The amount of share tokens to be minted."},"returns":{"assets":"The amount of assets consumed."}},"name()":{"details":"Returns the name of the token."},"owner()":{"details":"Returns the address of the current owner."},"pause()":{"details":"Pause user deposit and withdrawal operations."},"paused()":{"details":"Returns true if the contract is paused, and false otherwise."},"pendingManagementFee()":{"details":"Retrieve the amount of management fee share tokens that have not been minted yet."},"previewDeposit(uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC4626-previewDeposit}. "},"previewMint(uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC4626-previewMint}. "},"previewRedeem(uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC4626-previewRedeem}. "},"previewWithdraw(uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC4626-previewWithdraw}. "},"redeem(uint256,address,address)":{"details":"The asset redemption method of ERC4626, with the parameter being the amount of share tokens.","params":{"_owner":"The owner of the redeemed share token